1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,690
A robot needs to move this cup.
机器人要移动这只杯子。

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,250
The direct route is shorter.
直线路径更短，

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:06,650
It also runs straight into an obstacle.
却会撞上障碍物。

4
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,400
Before committing, could it compare the consequences
真正行动之前，它能先比较后果吗：

5
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,410
of going straight and going around?
直行，还是绕行？

6
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,990
That question gets us to world models.
这个问题把我们带到世界模型。

7
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,952
Welcome to DoF Infra, episode one.
欢迎来到 DoF Infra 第一期。

8
00:00:17,022 --> 00:00:19,592
Start with what the robot can observe:
先看机器人能够观测什么：

9
00:00:19,942 --> 00:00:23,132
camera images, joint positions, and recent actions.
相机图像、关节位置，以及最近的动作。

10
00:00:23,562 --> 00:00:25,752
A single picture may show where the cup is,
单张图像能显示杯子的位置，

11
00:00:25,822 --> 00:00:27,392
but not whether it is sliding.
却未必能判断它是否在滑动。

12
00:00:28,042 --> 00:00:30,032
History helps resolve that ambiguity.
历史信息有助于消除歧义。

13
00:00:30,382 --> 00:00:31,962
An encoder and a memory model
编码器和记忆模型

14
00:00:31,982 --> 00:00:34,172
turn that stream into an internal state.
将信息流变为内部状态。

15
00:00:34,562 --> 00:00:36,732
The state is learned, not a tiny photograph.
它是学到的表示，不是缩小的照片。

16
00:00:37,048 --> 00:00:38,868
Now hold the current state fixed
保持当前状态不变，

17
00:00:38,888 --> 00:00:40,618
and change the proposed action.
只改变候选动作。

18
00:00:40,848 --> 00:00:42,938
Push forward, or move around the obstacle.
向前推，或者绕过障碍物。

19
00:00:43,248 --> 00:00:44,508
A dynamics model predicts
动力学模型预测：

20
00:00:44,528 --> 00:00:46,698
how the state could evolve under each choice.
不同选择下，状态可能怎样变化。

21
00:00:47,048 --> 00:00:49,418
This action dependence is crucial for control.
依赖动作，是服务控制的关键。

22
00:00:49,688 --> 00:00:51,838
A policy answers, what should I do?
策略回答：我应该做什么？

23
00:00:51,968 --> 00:00:53,578
A world model helps answer,
世界模型帮助回答：

24
00:00:53,728 --> 00:00:55,358
what might happen if I do this?
如果这样做，可能发生什么？

25
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,510
Two imagined futures are not yet a decision.
想象出两个未来，还不能完成决策。

26
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,710
We need a way to compare them:
我们需要比较依据：

27
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:03,090
progress, reward, or distance to a goal.
进度、奖励，或与目标的距离。

28
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:05,700
In this illustration, the longer route wins
在这个示意图中，绕行胜出，

29
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,690
because the direct route collides.
因为直线路径会碰撞。

30
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:09,730
These scores explain the idea;
这里的分数用于解释原理，

31
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,730
they are not experiment results.
并非实验结果。

32
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:15,290
Execute a short step, look again, and update the plan.
先执行一小步、再次观察，然后更新计划。

33
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:18,510
A new observation can overturn an attractive prediction.
新观测可能推翻原本看好的预测。

34
00:01:18,910 --> 00:01:21,680
But where do useful predictions come from?
有用的预测从哪里来？

35
00:01:22,010 --> 00:01:24,420
DayDreamer learns from real robot experience,
DayDreamer 从真实机器人经验中学习，

36
00:01:24,610 --> 00:01:26,420
including awkward early attempts.
也包括笨拙的早期尝试。

37
00:01:26,810 --> 00:01:28,790
Its demonstrations include locomotion
演示包括行走，

38
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:30,660
and moving objects between bins.
以及在箱子之间搬运物体。

39
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:33,160
Each behavior is learned through interaction,
每种行为都通过交互学得，

40
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:36,220
not simply supplied by a general pretrained policy.
并非直接来自通用预训练策略。

41
00:01:36,605 --> 00:01:39,455
Follow the original figure from left to right.
沿论文原图从左向右看。

42
00:01:39,685 --> 00:01:41,875
Real observations train the state model.
真实观测训练状态模型，

43
00:01:42,125 --> 00:01:44,935
Then imagined state sequences train an actor and a critic.
想象状态序列再训练策略与价值评估器。

44
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:47,205
The actor learns which actions tend to pay off.
策略学会哪些动作通常更有收益。

45
00:01:47,225 --> 00:01:49,705
At execution time, it can choose an action
执行时，它可以直接选择动作，

46
00:01:49,725 --> 00:01:51,755
without searching a fresh tree of futures.
无需重新搜索一棵未来分支树。

47
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:54,715
So imagination can improve a policy during learning.
想象可以在训练阶段改进策略，

48
00:01:54,925 --> 00:01:56,485
It does not always mean the robot
但这并不总意味着机器人

49
00:01:56,505 --> 00:01:58,555
is planning online before every move.
每次动作前都在在线规划。

50
00:01:58,846 --> 00:02:01,596
TD-MPC2 takes the other route.
TD-MPC2 采用另一条路线：

51
00:02:01,886 --> 00:02:03,926
It searches candidate action sequences
搜索候选动作序列，

52
00:02:03,946 --> 00:02:06,896
in a learned latent space while the agent is acting.
在执行期间、在学到的潜在空间中搜索。

53
00:02:07,286 --> 00:02:09,336
Here the arrows predict the next state.
这些箭头预测下一状态。

54
00:02:09,846 --> 00:02:11,856
Reward estimates score the short rollout,
奖励估计评价短期展开，

55
00:02:11,986 --> 00:02:14,996
and a value estimate represents what may come afterward.
价值估计概括更远处可能得到的收益。

56
00:02:15,406 --> 00:02:17,316
Only the first action is executed.
只执行第一个动作，

57
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:20,236
The next observation starts another search.
下一次观测再启动搜索。

58
00:02:20,666 --> 00:02:23,576
There is no requirement to render every imagined frame.
不要求渲染每一帧想象画面。

59
00:02:23,923 --> 00:02:27,593
These TD-MPC2 clips are simulation benchmarks.
这些 TD-MPC2 视频来自仿真基准。

60
00:02:28,083 --> 00:02:30,213
They show manipulation and locomotion,
它们展示操作和运动控制，

61
00:02:30,403 --> 00:02:32,293
not a physical robot deployment.
并非真实机器人部署。

62
00:02:32,723 --> 00:02:35,433
Replanning limits how long we trust an old forecast.
重新规划缩短了依赖旧预测的时间，

63
00:02:35,823 --> 00:02:37,063
It cannot rescue a model
却无法自动修复

64
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:39,373
that systematically gets contact wrong.
一个始终把接触预测错的模型。

65
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:42,510
The prediction can also live in feature space.
预测也可以发生在特征空间。

66
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:45,340
V-JEPA 2 first learns from video,
V-JEPA 2 先从视频学习，

67
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:48,820
then its action-conditioned version learns from robot interactions.
动作条件版本再从机器人交互学习。

68
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:51,130
For planning, encode a goal image
规划时，将目标图像编码，

69
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:53,640
and compare it with predicted endpoint features.
与预测终点的特征比较，

70
00:02:53,850 --> 00:02:56,700
Search for actions that make those representations agree.
搜索让两者接近的动作。

71
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:59,740
The real robot examples use supplied goal images.
真实机器人案例使用给定的目标图像。

72
00:03:00,070 --> 00:03:02,730
The paper reports about sixteen seconds of planning
论文报告约十六秒的规划时间，

73
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:05,340
per action on an RTX 4090.
对应 RTX 4090 上的每个动作。

74
00:03:05,939 --> 00:03:08,989
RoboDreamer illustrates a different interface:
RoboDreamer 展示另一种接口：

75
00:03:09,379 --> 00:03:10,759
language and visual conditions
语言与视觉条件

76
00:03:10,779 --> 00:03:12,909
compose a desired video plan.
组合出期望的视频计划。

77
00:03:13,139 --> 00:03:14,829
Keep these two panels separate.
要区分这两个画面。

78
00:03:15,039 --> 00:03:16,489
One is a generated plan.
一边是生成的计划，

79
00:03:16,659 --> 00:03:19,429
The other is execution in the RLBench simulator.
另一边是在 RLBench 仿真中执行。

80
00:03:19,799 --> 00:03:21,749
Neither is proof of physical success.
两者都不能证明真实世界任务成功。

81
00:03:21,999 --> 00:03:25,069
A plausible movie, accurate action consequences,
看似合理的视频、准确的动作后果，

82
00:03:25,399 --> 00:03:26,599
and a reliable controller
以及可靠的控制器，

83
00:03:26,619 --> 00:03:28,589
are three different things to evaluate.
需要分别评价。

84
00:03:29,113 --> 00:03:30,623
Return to our cup.
回到这只杯子。

85
00:03:31,013 --> 00:03:33,333
The model might miss friction, hide an obstacle,
模型可能漏掉摩擦、忽略障碍，

86
00:03:33,353 --> 00:03:36,823
or underestimate how uncertainty grows over several steps.
或者低估多步预测中累积的不确定性。

87
00:03:37,213 --> 00:03:38,693
Test the action, the horizon,
要测试真正相关的动作、预测时长，

88
00:03:38,713 --> 00:03:40,703
and the outcome that actually matter.
以及实际结果。

89
00:03:40,933 --> 00:03:42,783
For grasping, inspect contact.
抓取要看接触，

90
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:45,463
For recovery, inspect motion after a disturbance.
恢复能力要看扰动之后的运动。

91
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:47,453
More realistic pixels are useful
更逼真的像素是否有用，

92
00:03:47,473 --> 00:03:49,843
only when they improve the task you care about.
要看能否改善你关心的任务。

93
00:03:50,053 --> 00:03:52,243
Measure that connection instead of assuming it.
这个联系需要测量，不能靠假设。

94
00:03:52,428 --> 00:03:55,118
When you open the next world-model paper,
下次打开世界模型论文，

95
00:03:55,288 --> 00:03:58,678
trace four things: its inputs, its predicted quantity,
追踪四件事：输入、预测对象，

96
00:03:59,028 --> 00:04:01,918
its decision rule, and its execution evidence.
决策方式，以及执行证据。

97
00:04:02,308 --> 00:04:03,608
Our DoF research map links
DoF 研究地图整理了

98
00:04:03,628 --> 00:04:05,678
the original papers and demonstrations.
原论文和演示。

99
00:04:06,028 --> 00:04:07,918
Follow the arrows back to the robot,
沿着箭头回到机器人，

100
00:04:08,108 --> 00:04:10,218
and ask what the prediction actually changed.
追问：预测究竟改变了什么决策？
